  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "10.8.1 -- a new color control, plus a full accessibility audit of the Edit* form controls (~75 findings) -- the counterpart to 10.8.0's UI-kit audit.\n\nNEW\n- EditColor: an AntDesign-5-style color field binding a plain string? -- swatch trigger, saturation/brightness area, hue slider, optional alpha slider, HEX/RGB input row, optional presets. Accepts hex (3/4/6/8-digit) and rgb()/rgba(); emits normalized lowercase hex. Read-only mode shows the swatch itself (plus hex text with ShowText). Backed by the new standalone UI-kit ColorPicker, the public ColorMath helper, and lazily-imported wss-color.js (keyboard and single-click work without JS).\n- Localizable accessible-name/announcement parameters across the library: FormLabel.TooltipTriggerLabel + IsRequiredTextIncluded, ReadOnlyValue/EditDisplay EmptyText, EditString show/clear button labels, radio OtherAriaLabel, Select live-region announcement formats + InputLabel/AriaLabelledBy, picker format/range hints and WeekLabel.\n- EditDate/EditDateRange gain RangeErrorMessage: an out-of-range typed date now raises a validation message instead of silently reverting (DatePicker.OnRangeError; per-endpoint on DateRangePicker).\n- EditFile gains a role=\"status\" live region announcing selection changes, and states its size/count caps up front in the drop zone.\n\nCHANGED\n- Auto-generated labels no longer shatter acronyms (URLPath renders \"URL Path\", not \"U R L Path\").\n- A field's accessible name now comes from its label's text alone (new lbltext-{id} naming anchor) -- a tooltipped field no longer announces \"More information\" as part of its name.\n- EditString's autocomplete fallback infers a real token from the property name (~20 common names) before the one-time-code last resort.\n- Contrast: --edit-color-border darkens to clear WCAG 1.4.11's 3:1; new *-strong tokens split text-grade from chrome-grade color uses; edit-controls.css gains its first Windows High Contrast (forced-colors) support.\n- EditDate/EditDateRange DialogLabel is now string? -- unset derives the dialog name from the field's own label.\n\nFIXED\n- A stale parse/range error on EditDate/EditDateRange now clears when the retyped value equals the one already bound (new OnValidCommit channel on both pickers, per-endpoint on ranges).\n- An invalid DatePicker/DateRangePicker field keeps its red error border on hover.\n- Select's combobox input now exposes its selected value; option groups now reach assistive tech.\n\nDEPRECATED\n- SelectOptionList.Tooltip is [Obsolete] and inert -- it repeated the field's tooltip on every option.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/dcblakesley/Controls#changelog",
